github.com/users/rivaratyr/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/rivaratyr/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-05-13T15:22:56Z", "updated_at": "2026-05-13T15:22:56Z", "body": "> [@rivaratyr](https://github.com/rivaratyr) I think this is resolved, correct?\n\nIn a way, yes. If you run `hermes update`, seemingly it fixes the error - even if you just freshly installed it.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/comments/4442563604/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/comments/4668356017", "html_url": "https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/10980#issuecomment-4668356017", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/10980", "id": 4668356017, "node_id": "IC_kwDOPRF1G88AAAABFkF1sQ", "user": {"login": "teknium1", "id": 127238744, "node_id": "U_kgDOB5WCWA", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127238744?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1", "html_url": "https://github.com/teknium1", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-06-10T08:56:19Z", "updated_at": "2026-06-10T08:56:19Z", "body": "<!-- hermes-sweeper:item=10980 -->\n<!-- hermes-sweeper:verdict=close reason=implemented_on_main confidence=high -->\nThis issue is resolved on current main \u2014 automated hermes-sweeper review.\n\n**Root cause:** The `APIConnectionError` regression was introduced by the keepalive/`http_client` change in PR #10933 (commit `12b109b66`). It was reverted the same day (commit `e07dbde58`) and then re-landed with regression tests as commit `8c478983e` (PR #11277, tests in #11266).\n\n**Evidence:**\n- Revert commit: `e07dbde582e6c80f80eb0d3040add8331832a87b` \u2014 \"Revert: enable TCP keepalives\u2026\"\n- Fix re-landed: `8c478983ed0ec5609212950d5044398dd4d27a5a` \u2014 \"fix: enable TCP keepalives to detect dead provider connections (#10324) (#11277)\"\n- `_build_keepalive_http_client` with platform-aware `SO_KEEPALIVE`/`TCP_KEEPIDLE` is live in `run_agent.py` lines 4817\u20134922\n- Regression tests covering multi-turn keepalive behavior added in `tests/run_agent/test_create_openai_client_reuse.py`\n- Fix shipped in **v2026.4.23** (released 2026-04-23)\n\nUsers on v0.9.0 who hit this needed `hermes update` as a workaround \u2014 that workaround is no longer necessary as of v2026.4.23. The commenter @sashamorozov correctly identified both the root PR and the revert commit.\n", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/comments/4668356017/reactions", "total_count": 1, "+1": 1, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}]